# Wave 14: fix accelerate/cos (docs.lammps.org/fix_accelerate_cos.html) drives an
# LJ liquid with a cosine acceleration A = 0.05 along x, z-periodic; compute
# viscosity/cos (docs.lammps.org/compute_viscosity_cos.html) gives the bias-free
# temperature (scalar, thermo_modify temp cos) and the 7-vector (six tensor
# components and the velocity amplitude V). fix temp/rescale uses the same
# compute through fix_modify temp, as the compute page describes for thermostats.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-7 abs=1e-9
units lj
atom_style atomic
lattice fcc 0.8442
region box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box 1 box
create_atoms 1 box
mass 1 1.0
variable vx atom 0.6*sin(1.7*x+2.3*y+0.7*z)
variable vy atom 0.6*cos(2.1*x-1.1*y+0.3*z)
variable vz atom 0.6*sin(0.5*x+1.9*z+1.3*y)
velocity all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
velocity all zero linear
pair_style lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
fix 1 all nve
fix 2 all accelerate/cos 0.05
compute cos all viscosity/cos
compute ke2 all temp
fix 3 all temp/rescale 10 0.6 0.6 0.02 0.5
fix_modify 3 temp cos
thermo_modify temp cos format float %.15g
timestep 0.005
thermo_style custom step temp c_cos c_cos[1] c_cos[2] c_cos[3] c_cos[4] c_cos[5] c_cos[6] c_cos[7] pe
thermo 20
run 100
